# Git's automatic line-ending conversion rewrites bytes on checkout. This
# project hashes files it ships: the embedded DcsEvalExecutor.lua carries its SHA-256
# into the binary, the installer gates uninstall on a hash, and the interop
# control asserts the shipped Lua's exact bytes. A Windows working tree with
# conversion on would break all three against a file nobody edited.
#
# Turn conversion off for everything. Files stay exactly as committed, on
# both platforms, and a hash means what it says.
* -text

# Shell scripts need LF whatever an editor does to them.
*.sh text eol=lf
